faqs=[('Why does my business need an IT audit?','An audit helps identify hidden security gaps, performance issues and infrastructure risks. PrismSuite turns these findings into prioritised recommendations for better technology decisions.'),('What does the PrismSuite audit deliver?','Five outputs: infrastructure health, performance, configuration assessment, data and network security, and an actionable recommendation report. Leadership receives a management-friendly summary alongside the technical assessment.'),('How does the audit work?','You complete a questionnaire, an ITCraft analyst gathers system information, PrismSuite analyses the findings, and the team discusses the report and next steps with you.'),('Which parameters are assessed?','Hardware and system configurations, installed software, storage, health, performance, availability and security posture. The current platform is described as using 200+ product benchmarks across 12 categories.'),('What happens after the report?','Findings are prioritised as Critical, High, Medium or Low. ITCraft discusses a structured action plan; the decision to proceed with implementation remains yours.'),('Is the initial audit free?','ITCraft offers a limited, one-time free IT audit to help SMEs understand infrastructure gaps. Contact the team to confirm availability and scope. Certification and specialist audit engagements are separate services.'),('How is remote access handled?','The audit workflow focuses on system-level information, rather than the contents of business documents. You may stay present during the session. Ask the team about the exact collection scope and available on-site options.'),('Do Apple devices need an audit?','Yes. Security and performance depend on configuration, software and the wider environment. An assessment considers the infrastructure as a whole, rather than assuming any device type is automatically secure.'),('Is PrismSuite a compliance certification?','No. It supports readiness by identifying infrastructure and security gaps. Formal certification and compliance audit services are scoped separately. ITCraft describes the PrismSuite assessment as valid for one year.'),('Do you offer VAPT or compliance audits?','Yes. Contact ITCraft to scope vulnerability assessment, penetration testing or certification-related audit requirements separately from the standard PrismSuite infrastructure assessment.'),('Which industries do you work with?','Manufacturing, pharmaceuticals, chemicals, logistics, banks and NBFCs, professional services, digital agencies and other organisations that depend on data and IT.'),('How can I become a partner?','The Authorised Tech Partner programme helps you introduce ITCraft to businesses in your network. It includes partner rewards and conversion commissions, with terms confirmed during onboarding. Explore the partner page to learn more.')]
